    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required enqueuing a welcome notification on successful owner creation, emitted via a logger named `NOTIFY` containing the owner id and memberId.\n\nIn `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` I made two changes:\n\n1. **Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger** alongside the existing `AUDIT` logger:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger NOTIFY = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\");\n   ```\n\n2. **Emitted the welcome notification** in `addOwner`, right after the owner is saved and the audit events are logged (so it only fires on a genuine successful create, not on rejects or idempotent replays):\n   ```java\n   NOTIFY.info(\"welcome owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n   ```\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` test \u2014 which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both the owner id and the fetched `memberId` \u2014 passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
